      "type": "item",
      "section": "Research & papers",
      "headline": "Carnegie Mellon steganography protocol reaches 94x the capacity of the prior art for undetectable agent collusion",
      "lines": [
        {
          "host": "A",
          "text": "Three researchers at Carnegie Mellon University built something called Codetta. It lets two separately deployed agents hide messages inside ordinary-looking output, and they report up to 94x the capacity of the best previous protocol for agents that don't share a model."
